# 13 The viscous term: an implicit solve {#ch:viscosity}

## Time discretisation

The `viscous_term` event advances
$$
\rho\,\partial_t\mathbf{u}= \nabla\cdot\left[\mu\left(\nabla\mathbf{u}+ \nabla\mathbf{u}^T\right)\right]
$$
with backward Euler ([section 7.5](07_cfd_concepts#sec:implicit)):
$$
\frac{\rho}{\Delta t}\mathbf{u}^{n+1} - \nabla\cdot\left[\mu(\nabla\mathbf{u}+ \nabla\mathbf{u}^T)\right]^{n+1} = \frac{\rho}{\Delta t}\mathbf{u}^{\text{old}},
\qquad (13.2)
$$
with $\rho$ and $\mu$ at $t^{n+\frac 12}$. Backward Euler is first order in time but
unconditionally stable. The unknown is the whole velocity vector because the
term $\nabla\mathbf{u}^T$ couples the components.

## Spatial discretisation

Write out the $x$ component of $\nabla\cdot[\mu(\nabla\mathbf{u}+ \nabla\mathbf{u}^T)]$ in 2D:
$$
\partial_x\left(2\mu\,\partial_x u\right) + \partial_y\left(\mu\,(\partial_y u + \partial_x v)\right).
$$
Each derivative of a flux is a difference of face values divided by $\Delta$,
like [(7.2)](07_cfd_concepts):
$$
\begin{aligned}
\partial_x(2\mu\partial_x u)\big|_{ij} &\approx \frac{1}{\Delta^2}\left[2\mu_{{i+\frac 12}}(u_{i+1} - u_i) - 2\mu_{i-\frac 12}(u_i - u_{i-1})\right],\\
\partial_y(\mu\,\partial_y u)\big|_{ij} &\approx \frac{1}{\Delta^2}\left[\mu_{j+\frac12}(u_{j+1} - u_j) - \mu_{j-\frac12}(u_j - u_{j-1})\right],\\
\partial_y(\mu\,\partial_x v)\big|_{ij} &\approx \frac{1}{\Delta}\left[\mu_{j+\frac12}(\partial_x v)_{j+\frac12} - \mu_{j-\frac12}(\partial_x v)_{j-\frac12}\right].
\end{aligned}
$$
The cross derivative $\partial_x v$ is needed on the horizontal face
$(i, j+\frac12)$, where no $v$ is stored. It is built from the four cell
centres around the face (figure 13.1):
$$
\Delta\,(\partial_x v)_{i,j+\frac12} \approx \frac{(v_{i+1,j} + v_{i+1,j+1}) - (v_{i-1,j} + v_{i-1,j+1})}{4}.
$$
The face viscosity is $\mu_{\text{face}} = f_m\,\mu(\bar f)$ with $\bar f$ the
average of the (smoothed) volume fraction of the two cells sharing the face
(`properties` event in `two-phase-generic.h`).

